      "cooked": "<p>I haven’t yet tried running a game of SCRPG, so bear with me for asking newbie questions. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"></p>\n<p>The Starter Kit and Core Rule Book make a pretty big point about having the players suggest/negotiate most twists; minor ones, anyway. Do the experienced GM’s find that players appreciate this feature or is it your experience that more players prefer to just “get on with it” and leave it to the GM to keep the action moving quickly?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
